---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const rules = [
  { t: 'Permission', p: 'Only people who signed up. No bought or rented lists.' },
  { t: 'A real identity', p: 'A verified sending domain and the sender\'s details in every email.' },
  { t: 'An easy way out', p: 'An unsubscribe link in every email, honoured straight away.' },
  { t: 'No repeat mail', p: 'Unsubscribes, bounces and complaints are blocked from future sends.' },
];
---
<Base
  title="Got an email sent with WebGen?"
  description="Who sent it, why it reached you, and how to stop it."
  path="/email/"
>
  <section data-section="quick" class="e-quick">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">For email recipients</p>
      <h1>Got an email sent with WebGen?</h1>
      <p class="lede">Here is who sent it, why it reached you, and how to stop it.</p>
      <div class="answer">
        <h2>Want to stop these emails?</h2>
        <p>Open the email and click <strong>Unsubscribe</strong> at the bottom. Click <strong>Unsubscribe</strong>, then confirm on the page that opens. You will not need to sign in. Many mail apps also show their own Unsubscribe button.</p>
        <div class="footer-mock" aria-label="Example email footer" role="img">
          <p>You are receiving this because you signed up at sunrisebakery.com.</p>
          <p><span class="unsub">Unsubscribe</span> · Sunrise Bakery, 12 High St</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-section="who">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Who sent it</h2>
      <p>WebGen is a website and email platform. Businesses use it to run their website and to email the people who signed up there. The email came from that business, not from WebGen itself. Their name and address are in the email's footer.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-section="why">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Why it reached you</h2>
      <p>Most likely you filled in a form on that business's website, such as a newsletter sign-up, a contact form or a free download. If the business asks new subscribers to confirm, you would also have clicked a confirmation link first.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-section="rules">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What we require of every sender</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        {rules.map((r) => <div class="card"><h3>{r.t}</h3><p>{r.p}</p></div>)}
      </div>
      <p class="muted">[CONFIRM: link to the acceptable use policy once written]</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-section="spam">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Think it is spam?</h2>
      <p>If you never signed up, tell us. Forward the email to <strong>[ABUSE EMAIL]</strong> as an attachment if you can, so we can see where it came from. We look into every report and stop senders who break our rules.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-section="help">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="helpbox">
        <div>
          <h2>Still need help?</h2>
          <p>A person will reply within [RESPONSE TIME].</p>
        </div>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/company/#contact">Contact us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  main > section { margin-top: 56px; }
  main > section.e-quick { margin-top: 56px; }
  .eyebrow { font: 700 .8125rem/1.2 var(--font-body); letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 12px; display: block; }
  .narrow { max-width: 760px; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.1875rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .answer { background: var(--tint); border-radius: 20px; padding: 28px; margin-top: 28px; }
  .answer h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; }
  .footer-mock { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px 16px; font-size: .9375rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .footer-mock p { margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .footer-mock p:last-child { margin: 0; }
  .unsub { color: var(--link); text-decoration: underline; }
  .grid { display: grid; gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 240px), 1fr)); }
  .card { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; padding: 24px; }
  .card h3 { margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .card p { margin: 0; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); margin-top: 20px; }
  .helpbox { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 20px; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: var(--surface); border-radius: 20px; padding: 28px; }
  .helpbox h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .helpbox p { margin: 0; }
</style>
